================================================================================
SAMPLING INTENSITY SIMULATION STUDY
Supporting Information Section S1.6
================================================================================

This folder contains the scripts used to produce the sampling intensity
simulation experiment reported in Section S1.6 of the Supporting Information
(Figures S3-S4, Tables S9-S11).

The experiment repeats the spatial misalignment scenario at four levels of
sampling intensity to assess how the number of sampling locations affects
estimation accuracy and predictive performance.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. DESIGN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

At each level, the true process is simulated over the unit square and
partitioned at random into a fitting set of M locations and a hold-out set of q
locations used to assess prediction. Within the fitting set, 80% of locations are
count locations and 20% are capture-recapture locations.

  Script     M     Count   CR     q     Total
  -------   ---    -----   ---   ---    -----
  M80.R      80      64     16    20      100
  M200.R    200     160     40    50      250
  M500.R    500     400    100   100      600
  M800.R    800     640    160   200     1000

All locations are sampled on all T = 6 occasions, so this experiment isolates the
effect of sampling intensity from that of temporal misalignment. Covariate
effects are spatially constant. Each level comprises 100 simulation replicates.

The M = 500 level is the spatial misalignment scenario reported in the main text
and reproduces it exactly.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. REQUIREMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

R version 4.4.2 or later.

R packages: nimble, sf, MCMCvis, coda, MASS, parallel

Run ../packages_needed.R first to install all dependencies. Note that climateR
and AOI are installed from GitHub via the remotes package; see that script for
details.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. HOW TO RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Run each script directly. Within each script, the two MCMC chains are run in
parallel on 2 cores.

    Rscript M80.R
    Rscript M200.R
    Rscript M500.R
    Rscript M800.R

Or source them from an R session:

    source("M500.R")

Each script runs all 100 simulation replicates sequentially. Because of the
computation times below, running M800.R on a high-performance computing cluster
is strongly recommended.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. COMPUTATION TIME
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Approximate wall-clock time per replicate (two chains in parallel):

    M = 80    0.11 h
    M = 200   0.19 h
    M = 500   0.90 h
    M = 800   4.47 h

Times for M = 80, 200 and 800 were obtained on an HPC cluster and the time for
M = 500 on a local workstation (Apple M4 Max, 48 GB unified memory), so they are
not directly comparable across levels. See Table S11 of the Supporting
Information for full details.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. NOTES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

NIMBLE emits the following warnings during model building. They are harmless
side-effects of how the m-array likelihood is specified and do not affect the
validity of the model code or the results:


    "dimensions specified are larger than model specification for variable 'Rm'"

Seeds are set from the global replicate number (1:100).


